          "evidence": "Independently reproduced every load-bearing claim with my own from-scratch code (re-derived the Fourier kernel chat_T from the integral definition, not copied). Scripts: 04-computation/verify_coset_quotient_adversarial.py, 04-computation/verify_pershell_fast.py; outputs in 05-knowledge/results/.\n\n(1) EXACT FACTORIZATION K(n)=D7(n mod7)/prod_j n_j for support-6 relations: max|K_indep - K_factored| = 1.7e-19 over 3000 random support-6 vectors. Both +A and -A sign conventions give identical D7 (6 factors -> (-1)^6=+1, as the claim's algebra predicts).\n\n(2) ANTIPODAL REALITY: D7(-c)=conj(D7(c)) to 7.9e-16. Verified the deeper mechanism: reciprocal sums satisfy S_{-c}=S_c (1/prod(-n)=+1/prod(n) for 6 coords), so each antipodal pair gives 2*Re D7(c)*S_c (real). Direct full COMPLEX correction at L=5 has Im=2.2e-16 -> correction provably real, not just empirically.\n\n(3) D7 SURVEY over all 6^6=46656 cosets: nonzero everywhere (min|D7|=1.69e-4), max|Re D7|=0.1431, max|Im D7|=0.627 -- exact match.\n\n(4) NEGATIVE DECAY ANSWER (the sharp part): k=8 AP exact target p0-M7=0.302731 (fractions.Fraction: p0=481/1470, M7=0.024480). Box-truncation recovers: L=3 -> -0.0365, L=5 -> +0.0626, L=7 -> +0.0821 (matches claimed 8.2%), L=9 -> +0.0655 (matches claimed 6.5%) -- NON-MONOTONE confirmed. Per-shell signed sums -0.001,+0.007,-0.017,+0.015,+0.015,+0.006 oscillate (no decay), exact digit match; per-shell absolute sums GROW 0.01->0.31->0.84->1.78->1.97. Conditional convergence and wrong-summation-order (MISTAKE-078) confirmed.\n\n(5) Envelope constant 0.6973 verified as the true max of |chat_T(m)|*|m| over ALL subsets T (single-sector |sin(pin/7)|/(pi|n|) peaks at 0.3103); internally consistent.\n\nCAVEAT (not a refutation): my independent per-shell ABSOLUTE sums are ~0.6x smaller than the verifier's quoted figures (relation-multiplicity convention across C(8,6) index-subsets); but the SIGNED sums and box-cum fractions -- the load-bearing quantities -- match